---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Matt Rabah, a CX, Customer Success, and Implementation professional focused on customer lifecycle systems, CRM discipline, and practical AI workflows."
>
  <section class="hero container">
    <p class="kicker">About</p>

    <h1 class="display">I build the operating layer.</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      My work sits between CX, customer success, implementation, CRM discipline,
      and practical AI.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section container" aria-labelledby="background">
    <header class="section-head">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="background">Background</h2>
    </header>

    <p class="about-prose">
      My background spans NeuroSync, Shinola, and Context By Design. The thread
      across that work is simple: customers feel the operating model. They feel
      the handoff, the missed note, the unclear owner, the delayed follow-up,
      and the moment a team has to rediscover what should already be known.
    </p>

    <p class="about-prose">
      I have worked across healthcare accounts, high-touch client experience,
      portfolio growth, Salesforce process, lifecycle diagnostics, onboarding,
      retention systems, and executive-facing account work. Different
      industries. Same underlying problem: customer experience breaks when
      ownership is vague.
    </p>

    <p class="about-prose">
      I hold an M.S. in Customer Experience Management from Michigan State
      University's Eli Broad College of Business, a B.S. in Organizational
      Behavior from Oakland University, and certifications across Salesforce,
      business intelligence, and inbound marketing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section container" aria-labelledby="focus">
    <header class="section-head">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="focus">Current focus</h2>
    </header>

    <p class="about-prose">
      My current focus is practical AI in customer-facing operations. Not AI as
      a novelty layer. AI as a way to reduce administrative drag, prepare
      better, surface risk earlier, and help teams make cleaner decisions
      without blurring accountability.
    </p>

    <p class="about-prose">
      Healthtech, medtech, and regulated environments are strong fits for this
      work because trust is fragile and implementation discipline matters. But
      the broader platform is customer lifecycle design for complex teams: clear
      owners, usable systems, better handoffs, and fewer surprises near renewal.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
